# OpenAI Agents SDK study app

A TypeScript learning project following Piyush Garg's 15-video OpenAI Agents SDK series. One folder per video in `src/NN-topic/`; the README "Learning topics" table tracks status.

## Stack
- Node 22, ESM (`"type": "module"`), TypeScript 6 strict (pinned `~6.0.3`; typescript-eslint doesn't support TS 7 yet), run with `tsx` (no build step)
- `@openai/agents` 0.20, `@openai/agents-core` 0.20 (only for `/extensions`), `zod` 4, `axios`, `dotenv`
- Default model: `DEFAULT_MODEL` (`gpt-5-mini`) from `src/constants`; never hard-code the model name

## Layout
Every folder exports through its `index.ts`; import from there.
- `src/NN-topic/agents.ts`: the lesson's agents (`new Agent({ name, instructions, model: DEFAULT_MODEL, ... })`)
- `src/NN-topic/index.ts`: entry point, one call: `await runChatLoop(agent, { context: DEMO_USER, intro })`
- `src/instructions/<agent>.ts`: one file per agent prompt (classifier prompts too). Every prompt is a function `export const build<Agent>Instructions: InstructionsBuilder = (runContext) => ...` (name the param `_runContext` if unused)
- One run context across the app: `UserContext` (`id`, `email`, `name`, optional `broadband: { customerId }`). Don't add new context types; add an optional property instead
- Agents are typed with their context (`new Agent<UserContext>(...)`) and every run passes it: `run(agent, history, { context: DEMO_USER })`
- `src/constants/`: app-wide constants (`DEFAULT_MODEL`, `USER_LOCATION`)
- `src/core/`: global auth and context: `UserContext`, `requireUser`/`requireCustomer` (throws if the user has no broadband account), demo logins (`DEMO_USER`, `DEMO_CUSTOMER`)
- `src/tools/<domain>/`: reusable tools, exported from `src/tools/index.ts`
- `src/guardrails/<entry|run|tool>/<domain>/`: guardrails, exported from `src/guardrails/index.ts`
- `src/shared/chat-loop.ts`: `runChatLoop` (readline loop, history, handoffs via `result.lastAgent`, guardrail tripwires, `input` option for `_try` scripts)
- `src/shared/log.ts`: `toPrettyJson` and `logRunItems` for tool and handoff logging

## Code style
- Double quotes, 2-space indent
- Imports across top-level folders use the `package.json` `"imports"` aliases: `#constants`, `#core`, `#guardrails`, `#instructions`, `#tools`, `#shared/<file>`. Export anything other folders need from the folder's `index.ts` rather than adding new aliases
- Imports within a folder stay relative and end in `.js`, even for `.ts` files (NodeNext): `import { getWeather } from "./service.js";`
- Use `import type` for type-only imports
- Every lesson file starts with `import "dotenv/config";`

## Commands
- `npm start src/NN-topic/index.ts` runs a lesson; `npm run check` (typecheck + lint + format check) must pass after every change; `npm run lint:fix` and `npm run format` auto-fix
- Chat lessons read stdin, so test them with a temporary `_try.ts` script, then delete it: either `run()` the lesson's agents directly, or call `runChatLoop(agent, { context, input: Readable.from(["question\n", ...]) })`. Don't pipe input into the chat loop from the shell.

## Safety
- Never read, print or commit `.env`; `.env.example` holds only a placeholder
- Before committing, check `git status` doesn't list `.env` or `node_modules`
